remoteClasses.doc:
Receives audio and video from a Media over QUIC (MoQ) relay into a Kurento media pipeline.
<p>
  Create this endpoint with the relay <code>url</code> and the
  <code>broadcast</code> name to receive. Call <code>subscribe()</code> to
  connect to the relay and make the decoded media available to the pipeline.
  Connect the endpoint to a media sink, such as a <code>WebRtcEndpoint</code>,
  to forward the received media. Call <code>unsubscribe()</code> to stop
  receiving.
</p>
<p>
  The endpoint uses the <code>moqsrc</code> element from the
  <a href='https://github.com/moq-dev/moq'>moq-gst</a> GStreamer plugin and
  decodes the received audio and video for use by Kurento. The plugin must be
  installed on the Kurento Media Server host.
</p>
<h2>Usage</h2>
<pre><code>
  // JavaScript (Kurento Client, callback API)
  pipeline.create('MoqSubscriberEndpoint', {
    url: 'https://cdn.moq.dev',
    broadcast: 'my-broadcast.hang'
  }, function(error, subscriber) {
    if (error) return onError(error);
    subscriber.connect(webRtcEndpoint, function(error) {
      if (error) return onError(error);
      subscriber.subscribe(onError);
    });
  });
</code></pre>
